  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In octahedral complexes, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> orbitals possess low energy as compared to <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> orbitals while in tetrahedral complexes <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> orbitals possess high energy as compared to <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> orbitals.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/71aad164-c7ea-4b31-8e2d-789f8c009ab9.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:3.4in;height:1.79167in\" />",
